    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0355" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4424: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McBride</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-01T18:00:00+01:00">September 1,
                            1943—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 2—10:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1519. From Murphy. Department’s 1593, August 30, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >1</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d343-f1"/> As stated in Fryer’s and my
                    previous telegram General Eisenhower has agreed to use of Camp Marshal Lyautey
                    as a site for refugees from Spain. All physical arrangements necessary to
                    provide for reception of the first batch have been concluded with military
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>I am continuing to urge upon Massigli<anchor n="25" xml:id="d343-f2"/> importance
                    of giving unqualified agreement to the proposal. Massigli again informed me
                    today that he would again ask Moroccan authorities to reply urgently. The French
                    have agreed in principle but may wish to impose certain conditions regarding the
                    length of stay, et cetera. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McBride</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d343-f1" n="24" xml:id="d343-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated that the Department would be pleased to have a report on
                    the status of negotiations with French North African authorities for designation
                    of site for refugees (840. Refugees/4423a).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d343-f2" n="25" xml:id="d343-f2-content">
                <p>René Massigli, French National Commissioner for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
